"There's not much more I can say than "Good bye,"
For my old life is drawing nigh;
My parents are gone, and that leaves just me;

‘The little old lady sat, and she looked at me;

And then her eyes did sparkle as they looked at thee;

She said: “I’ll give you all that I have got to thee—

So go with God on thy journey.”

I can remember well that day when we parted;
The joy I felt then, like an eagle’s heart,
Was torn out by your words to me so sad!

The world is one vast expanse Of life, and all things great and small ;
But none but Christ can make us one :

All our brethren are like to Him ;
By him their minds have been illumined

As I gazed around me,

I found an image most strange and new :

The stars they seemed descending swiftly ;

The first is to remember him, and the second — his work;

But how can I forget? No! How can he be forgotten?

While men speak who have never seen it or heard it tell.
